[{"id":"rx-order-steps","itemId":"uart-receiver","role":"warmup","promptHtml":"Put the steps of <code class=\"nobreak\">uart_rx</code> receiving one byte in order.","explanationHtml":"<p>The fall starts the start bit. Half a bit later the receiver stands in its middle, where a real start bit is still 0 and a short dip is already over. Each whole bit after that is the middle of the next bit: bit 0, bits 1 to 7, then the stop bit, which must be 1 for the byte to count.</p>","type":"order","steps":["Wait for the synchronised line to fall.","Wait half a bit, and check the line is still 0.","Wait a whole bit, and read bit 0.","Read bits 1 to 7, a whole bit apart.","Wait a whole bit, and check the stop bit is 1."],"shuffled":[4,1,3,2,0]},{"id":"rx-fill-shift","itemId":"uart-receiver","role":"core","promptHtml":"A UART sends bit 0 first. Fill in how <code class=\"nobreak\">uart_rx</code> takes the bit it reads into <code class=\"nobreak\">data</code>, so that after the eighth read, bit 0 is <code class=\"nobreak\">data[0]</code> and bit 7 is <code class=\"nobreak\">data[7]</code>.","explanationHtml":"<p><code>{line, data[7:1]}</code>: the bit just read goes in at the top, and the others move down one place. Bit 0, read first, moves down seven times and ends in <code class=\"nobreak\">data[0]</code>; bit 7, read last, stays at the top. <code>{data[6:0], line}</code>, shifting the other way, would turn every byte back to front.</p>","type":"fill","file":"hdl/level-10/uart_rx/uart_rx.sv","firstLine":57,"totalLines":67,"before":["  always_ff @(posedge clk)","    if (state == START) begin","      index <= 3'd0;","      data  <= 8'h00;","    end else if ((state == DATA) & mid) begin"],"blankLine":{"left":"      data  <= ","right":";"},"after":["      index <= index + 3'd1;","    end"],"highlighted":{"before":[[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"always_ff","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground