dmodule","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}]],"bugLine":33,"fixLine":"assign mid = (state == START) ? (timer == (LAST >> 1)) : (timer == LAST);"},{"id":"rx-choice-drift","itemId":"uart-receiver","role":"core","promptHtml":"The computer's clock runs 2% slow, so each bit it sends lasts 2% longer than <code class=\"nobreak\">uart_rx</code> counts. <code class=\"nobreak\">uart_rx</code> reads the stop bit 9.5 bits after the start bit's falling edge, by its own count. How far from the stop bit's middle is that read?","explanationHtml":"<p>Every bit's 2% adds up: by the stop bit's middle, 9.5 bits in, the read is 0.19 of a bit early, about a fifth. Reading in the middle leaves almost half a bit either way, so the byte still arrives. The synchroniser only delays the line by a cycle or two; it does nothing about the two clocks' speeds.</p>","type":"choice","options":["About a fifth of a bit early: still well inside the stop bit.","2% of a bit early: the error does not add up from bit to bit.","Half a bit early: it reads where the stop bit begins.","Not at all: the synchroniser takes out the difference."],"correct":0},{"id":"rx-fill-half","itemId":"uart-receiver","role":"core","promptHtml":"A bit lasts <code>LAST + 1</code> cycles. Fill in the count <code class=\"nobreak\">timer</code> must reach, after the start bit's falling edge, for <code class=\"nobreak\">uart_rx</code>'s first read to fall in the start bit's middle.","explanationHtml":"<p><code>LAST &gt;&gt; 1</code>, half of <code class=\"nobreak\">LAST</code>: half a bit after the edge. Every later read is a whole bit after the one before, <code>timer == LAST</code>, so each one also falls in the middle of its bit. Waiting a whole bit here would put every read at the start of the next bit.</p>","type":"fill","file":"hdl/level-10/uart_rx/uart_rx.sv","firstLine":32,"totalLines":67,"before":["  // Half a bit after the falling edge, then a whole bit after each read."],"blankLine":{"left":"  assign mid = (st